&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Vineyard 1 in Oxyrhynchite nome</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/aef6743f30/</link><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/aef6743f30/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="dates"&gt;Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;137 CE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;unexcavated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location unknown and size lost. Subleased in 137 CE for 4 years. Includes reed plantation (&lt;em&gt;καλαμεῖα&lt;/em&gt;) and rose garden (&lt;em&gt;ῥοδών&lt;/em&gt;). Surrounded by dikes and a palisade. Furnished with a sakiya (&lt;em&gt;μηχανή&lt;/em&gt;) operated by &lt;em&gt;hydroparochoi&lt;/em&gt; and using 5 oxen and 3 young cattle, a cistern (&lt;em&gt;ὑδροδοχεῖον&lt;/em&gt;) and with an open-air drying shed (&lt;em&gt;ἡλιαστήριον&lt;/em&gt;). Requires applications of &lt;em&gt;χοῦς&lt;/em&gt; and pigeon dung.&lt;/p&gt;
