&lt;p&gt;141 CE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;unexcavated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A reed plantation, orchard, and garden; location not preserved. Leased in 141 CE for a number of years now lost. Furnished with a sakiya, a small watchtower, and a walled animal enclosure. Requires applications of &lt;em&gt;χοῦς&lt;/em&gt; and dung. Rent includes cash, wine, fresh grapes, fresh and pressed dry dates, green and black olives, pomegranates, peaches, figs, myxes, two types of gourds, and vegetables (&lt;em&gt;λάχανα&lt;/em&gt;) according to season.&lt;/p&gt;
