&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Vineyard, orchard, and reed plantation near Tanais</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/cb3d3aa992/</link><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/cb3d3aa992/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="dates"&gt;Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;280 CE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;unexcavated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Near the village of Tanais, Oxyrhynchite nome. Size not stated. Work leased out in 280 CE. Orchard includes date palms and fruit trees (&lt;em&gt;ἀκρόδρυα&lt;/em&gt;). Surrounded by a mud-brick wall (&lt;em&gt;πλαστή&lt;/em&gt;). Furnished with an open-air drying shed. Watering required. Rent includes wine and various fruits: fresh and pressed dates, &lt;em&gt;καρυωτός&lt;/em&gt; dates, black olives, peaches (&lt;em&gt;περσικά&lt;/em&gt;), citrons (&lt;em&gt;κίτρια&lt;/em&gt;), summer and winter figs, and large white melons.&lt;/p&gt;
